{
  "openapi": "3.0.3",
  "info": {
    "title": "LendAutomate API",
    "description": "## Overview\nThe LendAutomate REST API enables third-party platforms to integrate with the private lending\nmanagement system. It provides programmatic access to all core modules: Leads, Deals, Loan\nServicing, Fund Management, Investors, Reports, Automation, and Administration.\n\n## Authentication\nAll API requests (except `/auth/login`) require a valid **Bearer token** obtained from the\nauthentication endpoint. Include the token in the `Authorization` header:\n\n```\nAuthorization: Bearer <your_access_token>\n```\n\nTokens expire after **24 hours**. Use the `/auth/refresh` endpoint to obtain a new token\nwithout re-authenticating.\n\n## Tenant Isolation\nLendAutomate is a multi-tenant platform. Every resource (leads, deals, loans, funds, etc.)\nis scoped to the authenticated user's tenant. You cannot access or modify data belonging to\nanother tenant.\n\n## Rate Limiting\nAPI requests are rate-limited to **1,000 requests per minute** per tenant. Exceeding this\nlimit returns HTTP 429. The response headers include:\n- `X-RateLimit-Limit` \u2014 requests allowed per minute\n- `X-RateLimit-Remaining` \u2014 requests remaining in the current window\n- `X-RateLimit-Reset` \u2014 Unix timestamp when the window resets\n\n## Pagination\nList endpoints support cursor-based pagination via `page` and `limit` query parameters.\nResponses include a `pagination` object with `total`, `page`, `limit`, and `totalPages`.\n\n## Error Handling\nAll errors follow a consistent structure:\n```json\n{\n  \"error\": {\n    \"code\": \"NOT_FOUND\",\n    \"message\": \"Lead with id 123 not found\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\nStandard HTTP status codes are used: 200 OK, 201 Created, 400 Bad Request, 401 Unauthorized,\n403 Forbidden, 404 Not Found, 409 Conflict, 422 Unprocessable Entity, 429 Too Many Requests,\n500 Internal Server Error.\n\n## Webhooks\nLendAutomate can push real-time event notifications to your endpoint via webhooks. Configure\nwebhook URLs in the Integrations module. Events include deal stage changes, payment postings,\ncapital call issuances, and e-sign completions.\n",
    "version": "1.0.0",
